# A user enum declaring `Ok`/`Err` cases is matched by its own cases when a call returns it; a fallible call's carrier is still matched by `.Ok`/`.Err`, also when the callee declares its failure and its success enum declares those cases.
fixture: a_user_enum_ok_names_its_own_case.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step o0: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "4\n0\nok 5\nerr none\n6\nnone\nnot an error\nhalf 4\nodd\nnegative\n"
stderr: empty
step o2: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "4\n0\nok 5\nerr none\n6\nnone\nnot an error\nhalf 4\nodd\nnegative\n"
stderr: empty
